  "problem": "The vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,\\,\\,\\text{_____},\\,5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\n$$\n\nparametrizes one sheet of the hyperboloid of two sheets defined in Cartesian coordinates as \n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25}=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nBy first considering the transformations\n\n$$\nx=6Z,\\,y=Y,\\,z=5X\n$$\n\nand writing the resulting system in cylindrical polar coordinates, determine the second component of $f.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that the hyperbola ${Z}^{2}-{r}^{2}={k}^{2}$ can be parametrized as $⟨Z,r⟩=⟨k\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,\\,k\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ⟩$* for $ϕ\\in R.$",
